      "title": "Deferred gain and basis follow the qualifying transaction",
      "narration": "Assume Rosa exchanges an annuity worth eighty thousand dollars with fifty thousand dollars of adjusted investment for a new annuity of equal value. The question states that all exchange requirements are met, with no cash received, debt, charges or other adjustment. The thirty thousand dollars of gain is not recognized currently, and the fifty thousand dollar basis carries into the replacement under these facts. It does not become eighty thousand dollars of fresh after-tax investment. Receiving cash or discharging policy debt can introduce taxable gain under additional rules. A life policy received in exchange for a modified endowment contract also retains that classification under the applicable rule. Check these features before using the simple example.",
